config DEFY_BT_HCI_SPI
    bool "Bluetooth HCI over SPI to the Defy's nRF52820"
    default y
    depends on DT_HAS_DYGMA_DEFY_BT_HCI_SPI_ENABLED
    depends on BT_HCI && BT_DRIVERS
    select BT_SPI
    select REBOOT
    help
      Zephyr's HCI SPI driver reworked for the Defy: no reset line, limited
      waits, data ready as a level, and power off with the RP2040.

config DEFY_BT_PERSISTENT_ID
    bool "Save the Defy Bluetooth identity before advertising"
    default y
    depends on DEFY_BT_HCI_SPI && BT_SETTINGS && BT_BROADCASTER && !BT_PRIVACY
    help
      Wraps bt_le_adv_start() to save the half's Bluetooth identity to
      settings before it first advertises with it, so that the half keeps
      its address across restarts and the Neuron's bond still fits. The
      wrap also lets half sleep hold off advertising while it shuts
      Bluetooth down.

config DEFY_RADIO_INSTALL
    bool "Install the radio firmware through Dygma's rf_bootloader"
    depends on DEFY_BT_HCI_SPI
    help
      Embeds the nRF52820 firmware from the radio build and, whenever the
      driver starts the radio, checks it in Dygma's rf_bootloader and
      installs it there if the radio holds anything else, as Dygma's
      keyscanner installs its own radio application. The build needs
      DEFY_RADIO_IMAGE_SOURCE, the C file scripts/package_radio.py writes;
      scripts/build passes it.
